# fixedbugs, defect 2036's finding, pinned 2026-10-13 as a known cost.
#
# SYMPTOM: a header of the program's own whose `printf("%+ d\n", 5)` gives
# both the `+` and the space flag is refused `ffi_header_refused` at exit 1,
# `flag ' ' is ignored when flag '+' is present [-Werror,-Wformat]`.
#
# REASON: C defines the call, C11 7.21.6.1p6: where the space and `+` flags
# both appear, the space flag is ignored; but clang files the diagnostic
# under `-Wformat` itself, under none of its parts, and the region keeps
# `-Wformat` an error for the conversion its argument does not match, which
# reads the wrong bytes (defect 2034); no pragma reaches one of its own
# diagnostics alone (`emit/header_region.hero`).
#
# RULING: the author's, 2026-10-13, a known cost: robustness first (design.md
# §1.12). Revisit if clang gives this diagnostic a flag of its own; this
# golden moves when the region can pass it over.

extern "fixedbugs-2036-a-header-s-printf-with-a-space-flag-beside-a-plus-is-a-known-cost.h"  #~ ffi_header_refused
    function fmt_shape() -> i32

function main()
    print(fmt_shape())
